sentences.l:
So he spoke, nor did the herald disobey him, having heard,
and set out to go through the people of the bronze-shirted Achaeans,
looking about for the hero Machaon;

for father Zeus will not be a helper of liars,
but those who first did harm beyond the oaths,
of them, indeed, themselves the tender skin the vultures will eat,

Why now do you stand thus, stunned, like fawns,
which, when they have tired of running over a great plain,
stand still, and no might at all arises in their wits;

sentences.t:
ἦ μένετε Τρῶας σχεδὸν ἐλθέμεν ἔνθά τε νῆες
εἰρύατ’ εὔπρυμνοι πολιῆς ἐπὶ θινὶ θαλάσσης,
ὄφρα ἴδητ’ αἴ κ’ ὔμμιν ὑπέρσχῃ χεῖρα Κρονίων;

sentences.tr:
ē menete Trōas schedon elthemen entha te nēes
eiryat’ euprymnoi poliēs epi thini thalassēs,
ophra idēt’ ai k’ ymmin hyperschēi cheira Kroniōn;

sentences.l:
but the others urge on, the long-haired-of-head Achaeans,
so that as quickly as possible we may fight, since they poured the oaths together,
the Trojans;
